      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1903, the Pittsburgh Reduction Company, later known as Alcoa, founded the town to support its mining operations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofbauxite.wordpress.com/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Bauxite Historical Association and Museum stand as a testament to the town’s rich heritage, hosting events and educational programs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofbauxite.wordpress.com/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During World War I, Bauxite’s ore production surged to 560,000 short tons, a peak driven by wartime demand.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
